### REST Client examples for World Cup Predictor API

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1) Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### 2) List all seeded teams
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Accept: application/json

### 3) Get one team by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/France
Accept: application/json

### 4) Get current authenticated user
# Requires a valid logged-in browser session (Google OAuth2).
# After logging in, copy the JSESSIONID cookie value from the browser and paste it here.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Cookie: JSESSIONID=your-session-cookie-here

### 5) List predictions for the authenticated user
# Requires a logged-in browser session.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/predictions?page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json
Cookie: JSESSIONID=your-session-cookie-here

### 6) Get one prediction by id
# Replace 1 with an actual prediction id from the list response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/predictions/1
Accept: application/json
Cookie: JSESSIONID=your-session-cookie-here

### 7) Create a new prediction
# Requires a logged-in browser session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/predictions
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Cookie: JSESSIONID=your-session-cookie-here

{
  "homeTeam": "France",
  "awayTeam": "Brazil",
  "matchStage": "Group Stage",
  "venue": "MetLife Stadium",
  "matchDate": "2026-06-16T18:00:00Z"
}
